  "format": "news",
  "script": "This iPhone isn't real. Neither is this color. And it's about to try selling you anyway.\n\nIt's an AI-made ad for the iPhone 18 Pro, in a shade called Dark Cherry that Apple hasn't announced. Only one thing about it is real.\n\nSo the creator, kaye dot creatives, built the phone, the lighting, the camera moves, using AI alone.\n\nAnd they said so in the caption: not a leak, just AI, labeled as AI.\n\n9to5Mac's Zac Hall watched it. He'd never cared for this color. This changed that.\n\nThat should worry Apple: a fake ad is outselling the real color.\n\nBecause Dark Cherry is a rumor, and the leaker who's seen the hardware says most renders have it wrong.\n\nIt's a deep purplish red, not the bright red everyone keeps drawing, tagged as Pantone 6076.\n\nSo it's reportedly replacing last year's hit, Cosmic Orange, as the one bold color choice this year.\n\nAnd a color Apple hasn't shipped has an ad, made by somebody who isn't Apple.\n\nThat one thing was real: it sold you too, on a phone that doesn't exist.\n\nNothing here is confirmed until Apple's event.\n\nThat's three days out, September 9th. The real phone has to beat the fake one. Think it can?",
